S="Joseph"
D("2026-11-09",S,"The Coat of Many Colors","a K–2nd grader, with help","Genesis 37:3",[(3,"Now Israel loved Joseph more than any other of his sons, because he was the son of his old age. And he made him a robe of many colors.")],
"Joseph’s dreams",[
"Jacob, who was also called Israel, had twelve sons. His favorite was Joseph, and he didn’t hide it. He gave Joseph a beautiful robe of many colors, and the other brothers didn’t get one. That made them jealous.",
"Then Joseph had two dreams. In one, his brothers’ bundles of grain bowed down to his bundle. In the other, the sun, the moon, and eleven stars bowed down to him. Joseph told his whole family about it. His brothers were furious. “Do you think you’re going to rule over us?”",
"The brothers hated Joseph so much they couldn’t even say a kind word to him. A family that should have loved each other was full of jealousy. But God had plans for Joseph’s dreams that no one could imagine yet."],
"Jealousy",["Jacob made a mistake by playing favorites, and Joseph made it worse by bragging. But the brothers chose to hate. Jealousy grows when we compare ourselves to others. God gives each of us different gifts, and He loves every one of His children completely."],
["What special gift did Jacob give Joseph? What bowed down in Joseph’s dreams?","Why were the brothers jealous? Have you ever felt jealous of a brother or sister?","Who did wrong in this story? How does jealousy grow in a family, and how can it stop?"],
"Heavenly Father, forgive us when we are jealous of others. Thank You for loving each of us completely.","Help our family celebrate each other instead of comparing.",
"Jacob gave Joseph a robe of many colors, and his brothers got jealous. But God had a plan!",
["Jacob had [twelve] sons.","Joseph got a robe of many [colors].","In his dream, the brothers’ grain [bowed] down.","The brothers were [jealous].","God had a [plan] for Joseph."],
["JOSEPH","COAT","COLORS","DREAMS","JEALOUS","BROTHERS"],[("Did Joseph’s brothers like his coat?",["Yes","No"],1),("What should we do when we feel jealous?",["Ask God for help","Be mean"],0)],
"Color Joseph’s coat with as many colors as you can!",("Genesis 37:3","“He made him a robe of many colors.”"),
scene(sun(560,56),hills(),coat(320),wheat(40,180),'<path d="M470,300 l20,-60 l20,60 M500,300 l20,-60 l20,60" />',label="Coloring picture: Joseph’s robe of many colors and bundles of grain"))

D("2026-11-10",S,"Sold!","an older kid","Genesis 37:4",[(4,"But when his brothers saw that their father loved him more than all his brothers, they hated him and could not speak peacefully to him.")],
"Joseph sold into slavery",[
"One day Jacob sent Joseph to check on his brothers, who were far away taking care of the sheep. When they saw him coming in his colorful robe, they said, “Here comes the dreamer! Let’s kill him and see what becomes of his dreams.”",
"Reuben, the oldest, convinced them not to kill him, so they tore off Joseph’s robe and threw him into an empty pit. Joseph cried for help, but they sat down to eat. Then a caravan of traders came by on the way to Egypt. Judah said, “Let’s sell him!” They sold their own brother for twenty pieces of silver.",
"The brothers dipped Joseph’s robe in goat’s blood and showed it to their father. Jacob thought a wild animal had killed Joseph, and he cried for days. Meanwhile, Joseph was carried off to Egypt as a slave. It looked like the worst thing that could happen. But God was still with Joseph."],
"When it looks hopeless",["Joseph was betrayed by his own family. Jesus was betrayed too, for thirty pieces of silver. In both stories, what looked like the end was really the start of God’s rescue plan."],
["Where did the brothers throw Joseph? How much did they sell him for?","How do you think Joseph felt in the pit? How did Jacob feel?","Compare Joseph being sold with Jesus being betrayed by Judas. What’s similar?"],
"Lord God, You were with Joseph in the pit and on the road to Egypt. Thank You that You never leave us, even when people hurt us.","When we feel betrayed or alone, help us trust that You are still working.",
"Joseph’s brothers threw him in a pit and sold him as a slave. But God was still with him!",
["The brothers called Joseph “the [dreamer].”","They threw him into a [pit].","They sold him for twenty pieces of [silver].","Joseph was taken to [Egypt].","God was still [with] Joseph."],
["PIT","SILVER","EGYPT","CAMELS","REUBEN","JUDAH"],[("Did God forget about Joseph?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who did the brothers sell Joseph to?",["Traders","Their dad"],0)],
"Draw Joseph in the pit, looking up.",("Genesis 39:2","“The LORD was with Joseph.”"),
scene(hills(),pit(320),person(150,beard=True,arms="mixed",hair="wrap"),person(500,beard=False,arms="open",hair="short"),label="Coloring picture: Joseph’s brothers by the empty pit"))

D("2026-11-11",S,"The Lord Was with Joseph","a 3rd–5th grader","Genesis 39:2, 21",[(2,"The LORD was with Joseph, and he became a successful man, and he was in the house of his Egyptian master."),(21,"But the LORD was with Joseph and showed him steadfast love and gave him favor in the sight of the keeper of the prison.")],
"Potiphar and prison",[
"In Egypt, Joseph was sold to a man named Potiphar, the captain of Pharaoh’s guard. Joseph worked hard and honestly, and the Bible says, “The Lord was with Joseph.” Everything he did went well, so Potiphar put him in charge of his whole house.",
"But Potiphar’s wife lied about Joseph and said he had done something bad. Even though Joseph did nothing wrong, Potiphar threw him in prison. Again, Joseph could have given up. But the Bible says it again: “The Lord was with Joseph.” Soon the jailer put Joseph in charge of all the prisoners.",
"Two prisoners, Pharaoh’s cupbearer and baker, had strange dreams. God helped Joseph explain them: the cupbearer would get his job back in three days. “Please remember me when you get out!” Joseph said. It happened just as Joseph said. But the cupbearer forgot all about Joseph, and Joseph stayed in prison two more years."],
"Faithful in hard places",["Joseph was a slave and then a prisoner for something he didn’t do. Yet he stayed honest and kept working hard. Twice the Bible says, “The Lord was with Joseph.” God doesn’t always take us out of hard places, but He is always with us in them."],
["Who bought Joseph? Where did Joseph go after someone lied about him?","How many times does today’s reading say “The LORD was with Joseph”? Why does that matter?","Joseph was faithful even when life was unfair. What does faithfulness look like when you’re treated unfairly?"],
"Lord God, You were with Joseph as a slave and in prison. Thank You for being with us in every hard place.","Help us be honest and faithful even when life feels unfair.",
"Joseph ended up in prison for something he didn’t do. But the Lord was with Joseph!",
["Joseph worked for a man named [Potiphar].","Someone told a [lie] about Joseph.","Joseph was put in [prison].","God helped Joseph explain [dreams].","The cupbearer [forgot] about Joseph."],
["PRISON","POTIPHAR","BAKER","CUPBEARER","DREAMS","FAITHFUL"],[("Did Joseph do something wrong?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who was with Joseph in prison?",["The Lord","No one"],0)],
"Draw Joseph helping in the prison.",("Genesis 39:21","“But the LORD was with Joseph.”"),
scene(bars(240,400),person(200,beard=False,arms="open",hair="short"),person(330,beard=True,arms="mixed",hair="wrap",s=.85),person(460,beard=True,arms="open",hair="curly",s=.85),label="Coloring picture: Joseph in prison with the cupbearer and the baker"))

D("2026-11-12",S,"Pharaoh’s Dreams","an older kid","Genesis 41:16",[(16,"Joseph answered Pharaoh, “It is not in me; God will give Pharaoh a favorable answer.”")],
"Fat cows and skinny cows",[
"Two years later, Pharaoh, the king of Egypt, had two dreams that scared him. In the first, seven fat cows came up out of the Nile River, and then seven skinny, ugly cows came and ate them up! In the second, seven full heads of grain were swallowed by seven thin, dried-up ones. None of Pharaoh’s wise men could explain them.",
"Suddenly the cupbearer remembered. “There’s a young man in prison who explained my dream!” Pharaoh sent for Joseph right away. They shaved him, gave him new clothes, and brought him before the king. “I hear you can explain dreams,” said Pharaoh. Joseph answered, “It is not in me. God will give the answer.”",
"Joseph explained: “There will be seven years of plenty, then seven years of terrible famine. Pharaoh should choose a wise man to store up food during the good years.” Pharaoh said, “Who could be wiser than you?” He put his ring on Joseph’s finger and made him ruler over all Egypt, second only to Pharaoh himself. In one day, Joseph went from prisoner to prince."],
"It is not in me",["Joseph could have taken the credit. Instead he pointed to God. That humility is a gift. And God’s timing was perfect: if the cupbearer had remembered sooner, Joseph might have been freed and gone home, and wouldn’t have been there for this moment."],
["What ate the fat cows in Pharaoh’s dream? What job did Pharaoh give Joseph?","Joseph said, “It is not in me.” Who did he give credit to? Why is that important?","The cupbearer forgot Joseph for two years. How did God use even that delay?"],
"Wise and powerful God, thank You for lifting Joseph up at just the right time. Your timing is always good.","Help us give You the credit for every good thing, and trust Your timing.",
"God helped Joseph explain Pharaoh’s dreams, and Joseph went from prisoner to ruler of Egypt in one day!",
["Pharaoh dreamed of seven fat [cows].","Joseph said, “It is not in me; [God] will answer.”","There would be seven years of plenty and seven of [famine].","Joseph would store up [food].","Pharaoh put his [ring] on Joseph’s finger."],
["PHARAOH","COWS","GRAIN","FAMINE","RULER","RING"],[("Who explained the dreams?",["God, through Joseph","Pharaoh’s magicians"],0),("How many years of famine?",["Seven","Two"],0)],
"Draw Pharaoh’s dream of fat cows and skinny cows.",("Genesis 41:16","“It is not in me; God will give Pharaoh a favorable answer.”"),
scene(pyramids(),throne(130),crown(130,140),person(130,beard=True,arms="open",hair="wrap",s=.9),person(280,beard=False,arms="open",hair="short"),wheat(380,620),label="Coloring picture: Joseph before Pharaoh with pyramids and grain"))

D("2026-11-13",S,"The Brothers Come to Egypt","a 3rd–5th grader","Genesis 44:33",[(33,"Now therefore, please let your servant remain instead of the boy as a servant to my lord, and let the boy go back with his brothers.")],
"Judah’s offer",[
"Just as God said, the famine came. There was no food anywhere, except in Egypt, where Joseph had stored up grain. Back home, Jacob sent ten of Joseph’s brothers to Egypt to buy food, but he kept Benjamin, the youngest, at home. The brothers bowed down before the ruler of Egypt. They didn’t recognize him, but Joseph recognized them. His dream had come true! Joseph spoke roughly to them and said, “Next time, bring your youngest brother, or don’t come back.”",
"When the food ran out, the brothers had to go back, and this time Benjamin came too. Joseph wanted to know if his brothers had changed. So he tested them. He secretly put his silver cup in the sack of Benjamin, Jacob’s new favorite. Then he had the brothers arrested. “The one who had my cup will be my slave. The rest of you go home.”",
"Years before, the brothers had sold Joseph without a second thought. But now Judah stepped forward. “Please, my lord, let me stay as your slave instead of the boy. If he doesn’t come home, it will kill our father.” Judah, who once said, “Let’s sell him,” now offered his own life to save his brother. They really had changed."],
"In someone else’s place",["Judah offered to take Benjamin’s punishment. Many years later, Jesus, born from Judah’s family, did that for all of us. He took our place and our punishment on the cross."],
["Why did the brothers go to Egypt? What did Joseph hide in Benjamin’s sack?","Why did Joseph test his brothers? How did Judah show he had changed?","Judah offered to take Benjamin’s place. How is that a picture of what Jesus did?"],
"Lord Jesus, thank You for taking our place and our punishment. Thank You for changing hearts, even the hardest ones.","Help us love our brothers and sisters enough to stand up for them.",
"Joseph’s brothers came to Egypt for food. Judah offered to be a slave so his little brother could go home!",
["The brothers came to Egypt to buy [food].","They [bowed] down to Joseph.","Joseph hid a silver [cup] in Benjamin’s sack.","The youngest brother was [Benjamin].","[Judah] offered to stay in his place."],
["FAMINE","BENJAMIN","JUDAH","CUP","GRAIN","SACKS"],[("Did the brothers recognize Joseph?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who offered to take Benjamin’s place?",["Judah","Reuben"],0)],
"Draw the silver cup and the grain sacks.",("Genesis 44:33","“Let your servant remain instead of the boy.”"),
scene(pyramids(),person(140,beard=False,arms="open",hair="short"),crown(140,114),person(270,beard=True,arms="open",hair="wrap",s=.85),person(360,beard=False,arms="open",hair="curly",s=.7),'<path d="M440,300 q-10,-40 16,-50 h30 q26,10 16,50 Z M460,250 l10,-10 l10,10" />','<path d="M530,300 q-10,-40 16,-50 h30 q26,10 16,50 Z" />',label="Coloring picture: Joseph’s brothers in Egypt with grain sacks"))

D("2026-11-14",S,"I Am Joseph","an older kid","Genesis 45:4–5",[(4,"So Joseph said to his brothers, “Come near to me, please.” And they came near. And he said, “I am your brother, Joseph, whom you sold into Egypt."),(5,"And now do not be distressed or angry with yourselves because you sold me here, for God sent me before you to preserve life.")],
"The reunion",[
"When Joseph heard Judah offer to take Benjamin’s place, he couldn’t hold it in any longer. He sent all his servants out of the room and began to cry so loudly that people in the palace heard him. Then he said, “I am Joseph! Is my father still alive?”",
"His brothers were terrified. They couldn’t say a word. This was the brother they had sold! But Joseph said, “Come close. Don’t be upset with yourselves for selling me. God sent me here ahead of you to save lives.” Then he hugged Benjamin and cried, and he kissed all his brothers.",
"Joseph sent wagons to bring his father Jacob to Egypt. When Jacob heard “Joseph is alive and ruling Egypt,” he could hardly believe it. At last, father and son met again. Joseph threw his arms around his dad and cried for a long time. The family that had been broken was together again."],
"Forgiveness",["Joseph had every reason to get revenge. He had the power to do it. Instead, he forgave. That kind of forgiveness only comes from knowing how much God has forgiven us. In Jesus, God doesn’t pay us back for our sins. He welcomes us close."],
["What did Joseph say to his brothers? How did they feel?","Joseph could have punished his brothers. Why did he forgive them?","Joseph saw God’s hand in his whole hard story. How can believing God is at work help us forgive someone?"],
"Merciful Father, thank You that You forgive us and call us close instead of paying us back. Thank You for bringing Joseph’s family back together.","Help us forgive each other the way You forgive us.",
"Joseph told his brothers, “I am Joseph!” and forgave them. The whole family was together again!",
["Joseph said, “I am [Joseph]!”","His brothers were [afraid].","Joseph said, “God [sent] me here to save lives.”","Joseph [forgave] his brothers.","Joseph hugged his father, [Jacob]."],
["FORGIVE","FAMILY","WAGONS","JACOB","HUG","TEARS"],[("Did Joseph get revenge?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who sent Joseph to Egypt to save lives?",["God","Pharaoh"],0)],
"Draw Joseph hugging his father Jacob.",("Genesis 45:5","“God sent me before you to preserve life.”"),
scene(pyramids(),person(200,beard=False,arms="open",hair="short"),person(270,beard=True,arms="open",hair="wrap"),'<path d="M440,300 h120 v-50 h-120 Z M450,300 a14,14 0 1 0 0.1,0 M550,300 a14,14 0 1 0 0.1,0" />',label="Coloring picture: Joseph hugging his father Jacob in Egypt"))

D("2026-11-15",S,"God Meant It for Good","Mom or Dad","Genesis 50:20",[(20,"As for you, you meant evil against me, but God meant it for good, to bring it about that many people should be kept alive, as they are today.")],
"Looking back",[
"Jacob’s family lived in Egypt for many years, safe from the famine. Jacob grew very old, blessed his sons and grandsons, and died. After the funeral, Joseph’s brothers got nervous. “What if Joseph was only being nice because of Dad? Now he might pay us back for everything.”",
"They sent Joseph a message: “Please forgive us.” Then they came and bowed down. “We are your servants.” Joseph cried again. “Don’t be afraid. Am I in the place of God? You meant evil against me, but God meant it for good, to save many lives.”",
"Joseph looked back over his whole life: the jealous brothers, the pit, slavery, the lie, prison, the forgotten promise. All of it had been painful. But God had been weaving every piece into a plan to save people. Joseph comforted his brothers and promised to take care of them and their children."],
"God works for good",["Romans 8:28 says, “For those who love God all things work together for good.” That doesn’t mean bad things are good. It means God is bigger than the bad things. The greatest example is the cross: the worst thing people ever did, God used to save the world."],
["What were the brothers afraid of? What did Joseph tell them?","Name the hard things that happened to Joseph. How did God use them?","“You meant evil, but God meant it for good.” How is the cross the biggest example of this?"],
"Heavenly Father, thank You for working in every part of our lives, even the hard parts. Thank You for the cross, where You turned the worst evil into our salvation.","Help us trust You when we can’t see what You are doing.",
"Joseph told his brothers, “You meant evil, but God meant it for good.” God can use even hard things!",
["The brothers were afraid Joseph would pay them [back].","Joseph said, “Am I in the place of [God]?”","They meant [evil].","God meant it for [good].","God used it to save many [lives]."],
["GOOD","EVIL","PLAN","SAVE","LIVES","TRUST"],[("Does God work even through hard things?",["Yes","No"],0),("Did Joseph forgive his brothers again?",["Yes","No"],0)],
"Draw the whole story of Joseph in four boxes: coat, pit, prison, palace.",("Genesis 50:20","“You meant evil against me, but God meant it for good.”"),
scene(pyramids(),coat(110),person(260,beard=False,arms="up",hair="short"),person(360,beard=True,arms="open",hair="wrap",s=.8),label="Coloring picture: Joseph in Egypt with his colorful coat"))
